---
title: Manual Admin Password Reset
description: Reset your admin password directly in the database when you can't use the normal reset feature.
sidebar:
  label: Manual Password Reset
  order: 3
---

Use this guide when you have lost admin access and cannot use the password reset feature. These steps use phpMyAdmin.

{% aside type="danger" title="Back Up Your Database First" %}
Back up your database before editing it so you can restore it if you make a mistake.
{% /aside %}

{% steps %}
1. Open Your Database

    Log in to phpMyAdmin and select your FOSSBilling database. You can find the database name in `config.php`.

    If you need help accessing phpMyAdmin, contact your hosting provider.

2. Edit Your Admin Account

    1. Click the **Structure** tab to see all tables
    2. Open the **admin** table

    ![Selecting the admin table](../../../assets/guides/admin-manual-reset/pma_table.png)

    3. Click the **Browse** tab to see all admin accounts
    4. Find your account and click **Edit**

    ![Clicking the Edit button on your account row](../../../assets/guides/admin-manual-reset/pma_row.png)

3. Set a Temporary Password

    The `pass` field needs a bcrypt hash. Generate one locally with Bash and PHP on a machine you trust. Do not use online hashing tools.

    ```bash
    IFS= read -r -s -p 'Temporary password: ' fossbilling_temp_password
    printf '\n'
    printf '%s' "$fossbilling_temp_password" |
      php -r 'echo password_hash(stream_get_contents(STDIN), PASSWORD_BCRYPT), PHP_EOL;'
    unset fossbilling_temp_password
    ```

    Enter a temporary password at the prompt. It will not appear on screen or in your shell history.

    1. Copy the generated hash
    2. Paste it into the **pass** field
    3. Click **Go** to save

    ![Pasting the hash and saving](../../../assets/guides/admin-manual-reset/pma_edit.png)

4. Log In and Change Your Password

    Log in with your temporary password, then change it:

    1. Click your name in the top right corner
    2. Go to **Profile**
    3. Switch to the **Change Password** tab
    4. Set a strong, unique password
{% /steps %}
